                    ║       PCBoard BBS 15.4 Revival       ║
                    ║                                      ║
                    ║     The Board That Wouldn't Die       ║
                    ╚══════════════════════════════════════╝

    Welcome to PCBoard 15.4 Revival — the community continuation of
    Clark Development Company's PCBoard BBS software.

    This release includes everything you need to run a PCBoard BBS
    in the modern era: all 12 original binaries rebuilt from source,
    plus pcbis.exe (PCBoard Internet Services) for telnet, BinkP,
    FTP, and HTTP access.


    WHAT'S IN THE BOX
    ─────────────────

    Disk 1 of 4 — Installation Disk
        INSTALL.EXE      PCBoard installer
        INSTALL.TXT      Step-by-step installation guide
        README.1ST       This file

    Disk 2 of 4 — Program Disk
        PCB154.ZIP       Main PCBoard executables (12 binaries)
        PCBSETUP.ZIP     Setup utility
        PCBSM.ZIP        System manager
        PPLC.ZIP         PPL 3.40 compiler

    Disk 3 of 4 — Documentation Disk
        FEATURES.TXT     What's new in 15.4 Revival
        UPGRADE.TXT      Upgrade guide from 15.2/15.3
        WHATSNEW.TXT     Detailed change log
        SYSGUIDE.ZIP     Sysop's reference guide
        CALGUIDE.ZIP     Caller's guide

    Disk 4 of 4 — Internet Server
        PCBIS.EXE        PCBoard Internet Services daemon
        PCBIS.CFG        Sample configuration
        PCBIS.TXT        Internet Services administrator guide
        INDEX.HTM        Default BBS web page


    QUICK START
    ───────────

    New Installation:
        1. Run INSTALL.EXE from Disk 1
        2. Insert Disk 2 when prompted (or point to disk2/ directory)
        3. Run PCBSETUP to configure your board
        4. Run PCBIS to accept telnet connections (see Disk 4)
        5. Read FEATURES.TXT on Disk 3 for what's new

    Upgrade from 15.2 or 15.3:
        1. BACK UP YOUR EXISTING INSTALLATION
        2. Read UPGRADE.TXT on Disk 3
        3. Run INSTALL.EXE and choose Upgrade
        4. Review WHATSNEW.TXT for changes that affect your setup

    Running with Internet Access:
        1. Copy PCBIS.EXE and PCBIS.CFG from Disk 4
        2. Edit PCBIS.CFG with your settings (ports, paths, addresses)
        3. Run PCBIS — it handles telnet, FTP, HTTP, and BinkP
        4. No FOSSIL driver needed — pcbis bridges TCP directly


    SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
    ───────────────────

    DOS PCBoard:
        386 or higher processor
        4MB RAM minimum (8MB recommended)
        DOS 5.0 or higher, or OS/2 2.1+
        Hard disk with 10MB free space

    pcbis Internet Services:
        Linux x86 or x86_64 (recommended for server use)
        OR DOS/OS/2 with TCP/IP stack
        Network connection
        Open ports: 2323 (telnet), 24554 (BinkP), 21 (FTP), 8080 (HTTP)


    PROVENANCE
    ──────────

    PCBoard was created by Fred Clark and Clark Development Company,
    Inc. of Murray, Utah. Over 50,000 licenses were sold between
    1983 and 1997.

    The 15.3 source code was preserved by PWA (Pirates With Attitude)
    from the only source license known to have been sold, purchased
    by Corey Blake. Without this preservation, no PCBoard source
    code would exist today.

    15.4 Revival applies all features and fixes from Clark's
    unreleased 15.4b beta, rebuilds every binary from source using
    open toolchains (OpenWatcom, no Borland dependency), and adds
    internet services for the modern era.

    Source code: https://github.com/verta1878/pcbrevival


    CREDITS
    ───────

    Original PCBoard:     Fred Clark, Clark Development Company
